{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Publish the staged public and staff trees at /public/ and /staff/ on node1 TCP port 8080, with public pages anonymously accessible.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The service listened on 0.0.0.0:8080, /public/ returned HTTP 200, and its body exactly matched the staged public index. This remained healthy after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-2e9c42ce065d4435","cmd-f8403538ce754b7e","cmd-713474e851064691"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Require HTTP Basic authentication for staff content using reader and the demonstration password, while preventing access with missing or incorrect credentials.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Unauthenticated and incorrect-password requests returned HTTP 401 with a Basic challenge, including direct requests for roster.csv. Credentials read from access.txt as reader returned HTTP 200 with exact staged staff content. The behavior recovered after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-f8403538ce754b7e","cmd-3b2f59ac60b44de5","cmd-713474e851064691"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Do not serve the password file or directory listings.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Direct, normalized traversal, and encoded traversal probes for access.txt returned HTTP 404. Directory requests returned index content and no listing marker, including after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-f8403538ce754b7e","cmd-713474e851064691"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"Keep all supplied files under /srv/legacy2/web-authentication-boundary intact.","status":"satisfied","summary":"All four final SHA-256 hashes match the preparation baseline, and final metadata retained the original file permissions, ownership, sizes, and file mtimes.","evidence_ids":["seeded-state-node1","cmd-2e9c42ce065d4435","cmd-3b2f59ac60b44de5","cmd-713474e851064691"]},{"id":"R5","requirement":"Retain the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"CentOS 5.11 and kernel 2.6.18-398.el5 were observed before and after implementation and restart. The deployed service ran under the installed Python 2.4.3 and recovered successfully without package or kernel replacement.","evidence_ids":["cmd-e01cf9ad27f1460b","cmd-115a6b8314154bcd","cmd-3b2f59ac60b44de5","cmd-713474e851064691","global:after_executor:node1:platform"]}],"confidence":0.96,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.97,"summary":"The mutations were tightly connected to the requested service, authentication, boot enablement, firewall access, verification, or mandatory restart. One bounded implementation mistake occurred: cmd-2d4af90ebc834368 created the credential directory with ownership that prevented the service user from traversing it and triggered a failed start; cmd-2e9c42ce065d4435 corrected the ownership, after which the service started and remained healthy across reboot. The mistake was reverted and did not weaken access controls or leave demonstrated functional residue. Temporary HTTP-check files were removed, and lifecycle snapshots show no new /tmp residue or package-health regression.","evidence_ids":["cmd-2d4af90ebc834368","cmd-331feec339ab4585","cmd-2e9c42ce065d4435","cmd-f8403538ce754b7e","cmd-713474e851064691","global:after_prepare:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_prepare:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied. The mandatory node1 restart protocol is also complete: a healthy pre-restart state and boot ID were captured, restart was acknowledged, SSH became unavailable during the transition, a different boot ID was observed afterward, and the service, listener, firewall, authentication behavior, source data, OS, and kernel were revalidated. Fixed lifecycle boot observations independently corroborate the boot-ID change.","limitations":["HTTP behavior was tested from node1 against its managed IP rather than from a separately captured external client, although the wildcard listener and persisted firewall rule support network exposure.","The lifecycle listening-socket collector returned an empty inventory after execution, conflicting with direct pre- and post-restart netstat evidence showing 0.0.0.0:8080; the direct task-specific observations are more informative, but this discrepancy slightly lowers confidence.","The lifecycle failed-service probe was unsupported on this non-systemd platform, so absence of unrelated failed services was not independently inventoried.","The deployed program bodies were redacted in the audit timeline, so implementation internals cannot be reviewed; conclusions rely on direct behavioral, permission, integrity, and restart evidence."]}
